**user**:
> I am trying to serve a PDF within a shiny app. I have a PDF in a www directory:% lsapp-test.Rapp2.Rdeploy.Rpicker_test.Rtestit.R~app-test.R~app2.R~deploy.R~rsconnectwwwapp.Rchannelslibshapefilesapp.R~Dataset v2output-v2testit.R% ls wwwPROSPER_Technical_Documentation.pdfBut both of these links show "Not Found":http://127.0.0.1:6568/www/PROSPER_Technical_Documentation.pdfhttp://127.0.0.1:6568/PROSPER_Technical_Documentation.pdf
> 
> The app s running:> shinyApp(ui, server)Listening on http://127.0.0.1:6568
**assistant**:
> `www/` is normally served at the app root, so the expected URL is:
> 
> ```text
> http://127.0.0.1:6568/PROSPER_Technical_Documentation.pdf
> ```
> 
> —not `/www/...`.
> 
> However, when launching an app directly with `shinyApp(ui, server)`, Shiny may not automatically register the local `www` directory as an app resource path. Explicitly register it:
> 
> ```r
> library(shiny)
> 
> addResourcePath(
>   prefix = "docs",
>   directoryPath = normalizePath("www")
> )
> 
> ui <- fluidPage(
>   tags$a(
>     "Technical documentation",
>     href = "docs/PROSPER_Technical_Documentation.pdf",
>     target = "_blank"
>   )
> )
> 
> server <- function(input, output, session) {}
> 
> shinyApp(ui, server)
> ```
> 
> Then this should work:
> 
> ```text
> http://127.0.0.1:6568/docs/PROSPER_Technical_Documentation.pdf
> ```
> 
> `addResourcePath()` is especially useful if you run the app from a script or a working directory other than the app directory. `normalizePath("www")` also ensures Shiny receives an absolute filesystem path.
